# Usage

The JXR Plugin generates a cross-reference of the project's sources. Below are the different goals and configurations for the plugin.

Generate JXR as Part of Project Reports
---------------------------------------

To include the JXR report in the site generation process, insert the following in the `<reporting>` section of your `pom.xml`:

```xml
<project>
  ...
  <build>
    ...
  </build>
  <reporting>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-jxr-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </reporting>
  ...
</project>
```

The report will be generated when you execute:

```shell
mvn site
```

Explicitly Generate JXR Files
-----------------------------

The JXR files for the project's main sources will be generated using this command:

```shell
mvn jxr:jxr
```

To generate JXR files for the project's test sources, execute this command:

```shell
mvn jxr:test-jxr
```

Navigate with Frames or with a Search Box
-----------------------------------------

The pages of the report are modelled on those of Javadoc. Which Javadoc that is depends on the `javadocVersion` parameter, and by default it is the one of the Java version that runs the build.

Javadoc removed frames in Java 13. As of version 3.7.0 the JXR report does the same from that Java version on: every page has a navigation bar, with a search box in it that finds the packages and classes of the project by their name. To get the frames back, ask for the templates of an older Javadoc in the configuration of the plugin:

```xml
<project>
  ...
  <reporting>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-jxr-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          <javadocVersion>1.8</javadocVersion>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </reporting>
  ...
</project>
```

The `<reporting>` section counts when the report is generated with the site (`mvn site`). If you run `mvn jxr:jxr` directly, put the same `<configuration>` into `<build><pluginManagement>` instead.

**Note**: Prefer the configuration in the POM over `-DjavadocVersion=1.8` on the command line when the Javadoc Plugin runs in the same build. It has a parameter with the same user property, where it stands for the version of the Javadoc tool.
